   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1942-01-30">January 30, 1942</date>.</dateline>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Doctor
                  Tillich</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>I have read over carefully your three articles in THE PROTESTANT. As a political
               philosophy they really express the best in the American ideal but I do not see that
               they are connected particularly with the Christian religion except that they are
               printed in a religious publication.</p>
            <p>It seems to me that you expressed in an authoritative way the philosophy which the
               United States government has since picked up because of the war effort and gradually
               out of this <hi rend="underline">is</hi> coming the war aims.</p>
            <p>Your comments on the social changes seem to be the general trend. The idea of the
               peace conference that can attain social, political and intellectual structure of life
               in which the conditions of the present catastrophe are overcome is the ideal of
               democracy. Are democracy and Christianity synonymous?</p>
            <p>I enjoyed these articles very much.</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Very sincerely yours,</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4254" type="person"
                  ><hi rend="hand">Wilson Parkhill</hi></rs></signed>
               WP W
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
